    {
      "id": "fb-004",
      "question": "What is IVMS?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 25.27,
      "answer": "IVMS is a vehicle telematics system that provides core functionalities such as location tracking, trip history, and geofencing. It can be enhanced with add-ons like driver behavior monitoring (ECO) and business intelligence dashboards. The system is designed to ensure stable tracking, compliance, and readiness for reporting by applying baseline alerts and reports such as overspeed, ignition on/off, geofence in/out, daily trips, stops, mileage, and driver behavior summaries.\n\nSource: NAVAS CMS User Manual — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
