      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 26.06,
      "answer": "Tracking tokens in the NAVAS ecosystem are part of a consumption-based billing structure. They allow for low-cost, mass-market tracking of vehicles, fuel, drivers, equipment, and staff in real-time. This system is designed to be flexible and scalable, accommodating various tracking needs through different modules like Piki, Oliwa, Patrol, UKO, and VEBA.\n\nSource: Sales Procedures 3DS-QMS-PR-09 ver26 (Uganda & Kenya) — this is the documented procedure; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
